Changes:
* June 2021: John Robertson (independent) resigns from council<ref>{{cite news |last1=Robertson |first1=Ross |title=Independent councillor quits in dramatic resignation - but says he'll stand again in by-election to fill the vacancy |url=https://www.shieldsgazette.com/news/politics/council/independent-councillor-quits-in-dramatic-resignation-3269700 |access-date=10 April 2022 |work=Shields Gazette |date=11 June 2021 |language=en}}</ref>
* July 2021: Jay Potts wins by-election for Labour from independent,<ref>{{cite news |last1=Binding |first1=Chris |title=Labour wins Fellgate and Hedworth by-election as John Robertson fails to reclaim seat after resignation |url=https://www.shieldsgazette.com/news/politics/council/labours-jay-potts-wins-fellgate-and-hedworth-by-election-as-john-robertson-fails-to-reclaim-seat-after-resignation-3328616 |access-date=10 April 2022 |work=Shields Gazette |date=29 July 2021 |language=en}}</ref> Jeff Milburn (independent) disqualified from council<ref>{{cite news |last1=Binding |first1=Chris |title=Councillor who carried knife to court is 'disqualified' |url=https://www.chroniclelive.co.uk/news/north-east-news/south-tyneside-councillor-jeff-milburn-21128730 |access-date=10 April 2022 |work=ChronicleLive |date=23 July 2021 |language=en}}</ref>
* September 2021: Stan Wildhirt wins by-election for Conservatives from independent<ref>{{cite news |last1=Robertson |first1=Ross |title=Conservatives win the Cleadon and East Boldon by-election - these are the full results |url=https://www.shieldsgazette.com/news/politics/council/conservatives-win-the-cleadon-and-east-boldon-by-election-3377926 |access-date=10 April 2022 |work=Shields Gazette |date=9 September 2021 |language=en}}</ref>
* February 2022: Rob Dix (Labour) dies; seat left vacant until May election<ref>{{cite news |last1=Brownson |first1=Sophie |title=Tributes to South Shields Labour councillor Rob Dix after sudden death |url=https://www.chroniclelive.co.uk/news/north-east-news/south-shields-rob-dix-death-23044724 |access-date=10 April 2022 |work=ChronicleLive |date=9 February 2022 |language=en}}</ref>

